## Deploying

```bash
docker build -t {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %} .
docker run --rm -v {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %}-data:/data {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %} app db migrate   # before rolling out
docker run -p 8000:8000 -v {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %}-data:/data {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %}
```

Before the first deploy:

- **Authentication.** The `X-User-Id` header authenticator only runs locally; a deployed
  app refuses to start until you pass a real `Authenticator` (for example, OIDC token
  verification) to `make_app` in [main.py](src/{% endraw %}{{ package_name }}{% raw %}/main.py).
{% endraw %}{% if database == "sqlite" %}{% raw %}- **Database.** SQLite serves a single machine well: one writer at a time, many readers,
  with write-ahead logging on. The image keeps it at `/data/{% endraw %}{{ package_name }}{% raw %}.db`; mount durable
  storage there (`-v {% endraw %}{{ project_name }}{% raw %}-data:/data`) and back the file up. If you outgrow one
  machine, switch `{% endraw %}{{ env_prefix }}{% raw %}_DATABASE_URL` to Postgres and add `psycopg[binary]`.
{% endraw %}{% endif %}{% if database == "postgres" %}{% raw %}- **Database.** Point `{% endraw %}{{ env_prefix }}{% raw %}_DATABASE_URL` at Postgres.
{% endraw %}{% endif %}{% raw %}- **Schema.** Create a new database with `app db create`; upgrade existing ones with
  `app db migrate`.
- **Proxies.** Behind a load balancer, set `{% endraw %}{{ env_prefix }}{% raw %}_FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` to its address
  range so client addresses and the request scheme come through.
- **Probes.** `/health` answers while the process is up; `/ready` also checks the database.
- **Metrics.** Set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` to export to an OpenTelemetry collector.

